2026-09-12 — retire check_theory
================================

Remove check_theory: it was never distinct from load_theory. Both methods
called the identical use_theories_result with identical parameters
(mcp_session.scala), and calling load_theory then check_theory on the same
theory with the same arguments produced byte-identical replies against the
running server. load_theory already re-reads the theory file fresh on every
call, which is the whole of what check_theory's "re-check after an edit"
framing needed. No shim; the server now advertises seven Scala builtins.
Removing the reserved name also frees "check_theory" for a community
mcp_tool declaration. check_theory#T1-T4's claims migrate to
load_theory#T7-T10 (plans/load_theory); plans/check_theory is deleted.

2026-09-10 — approved server carve-out
====================================

Reduce the public server to the eight Scala builtins documented in README and
extensible ML tools. Remove resources and their twins, mutable scopes, all REPL
implementations, old proof search/navigation and the IR bridge/engine.

Use the fresh startup-root catalogue to select ML tools and ML target resolvers
for invocation contexts. Preserve declaration notifications, activation, HOL-safe
registration, readiness, generic bridge and lifecycle/output protections.

Remove obsolete active plans, evaluations and documentation instead of retaining
compatibility copies. Earlier implementation history remains in Git. This entry
records the authorized change, not a claim that runtime acceptance has passed.

Approved follow-up: own a live PIDE root from bootstrap to shutdown, require its
successful final end before Ready, retain its document requirement, and drain
before release/stop with no heap-root fallback. The mandatory root_node/root_command/root_exec selector is approved for every
hello/call using existing Isabelle APIs and no prover-source patches. The missing baseline request-byte guard is explicitly
deferred; retiring its old T11 obligation does not claim implementation or a
passing protection. Actual reply bounds remain required.

Root ownership clarification: always use a private temporary live PIDE wrapper
importing exactly the configured -T theory, uniformly for image and source.
Catalogue and default execution use the wrapper context; ancestor/wrapper
reprocessing updates later calls. Every hello/call carries mandatory root_node/root_command/root_exec beside theory
identity; ML validates the current completed final-end evaluation. Invalid/stale
selectors fail without fallback. This records approval, not runtime completion.
